# Keep the image small: ship only what the static site needs.
.git
.gitignore
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose.yml
.venv/
venv/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
README.md
docs/
# The analyser submodule now serves itself entirely (frontend + API) from the
# analyser container (see deploy/docker-compose*.yml) -- the web/nginx image
# never needs its files, it only reverse-proxies to it.
analyser/
tests/
samples/
archive/
screenshots/
# Remotion video source (not served, no runtime dependency on the site).
site/video-src/
# `COPY . .` puts the build context into the public web root, so anything not
# excluded here becomes downloadable at https://vahinitech.com/<path>. Ship
# only /site plus the nginx configs the Dockerfile installs into /etc/nginx
# (those never land in the web root -- and nginx blocks /deploy/* regardless).
deploy/*
!deploy/nginx.conf
!deploy/nginx-security.conf
!deploy/nginx-headers.inc
# Defense in depth: even if deploy/ exclusions above are ever loosened, never
# let a real, locally-created Cloudflare API token leak into the image.
deploy/certbot/cloudflare-credentials.ini
# The persist-api Dockerfile's build context is also the repo root (see
# deploy/docker-compose.prod.yml / root docker-compose.yml), so this file
# must NOT exclude services/ -- that would also strip persist-api's own
# source from its own build. services/persist-api/Dockerfile.dockerignore
# (BuildKit's per-Dockerfile override, which fully replaces this file for
# that build) is where persist-api's context is scoped down instead. nginx
# also blocks public /services/ regardless (deploy/nginx.conf), so the web
# image not shipping it is belt-and-suspenders, not the only protection.
services/
tools/
node_modules/
package.json
package-lock.json
sbom.spdx.json
Makefile
Dockerfile.npm-test
THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md
uploads/
shots/
scraps/
.thumbnail
.image-slots.state.json
*.md
scan-reports/
